    <xcal:components>
      <xcal:vevent>
        <xcal:properties>
          <xcal:comment>
            <xcal:text>Event part mostly exists to make this a "compliant" entry. Otherwise, this entry only exists to provide one instance of each known data-type as a property on the surrounding calendar object.
GEO, VERSION, and REQUEST-STATUS are added to the calendars properties, since those have special handling, but no VALUE parameter to specify that such handling should occur. Likewise, X-UNKNOWN lacks a VALUE parameter, and should be parsed as an unknown (and therefore opaque) type.</xcal:text>
          </xcal:comment>
